---
title: "What does the HUD list?"
accTitle: "Section HUD windowing rule"
accDescr: "Notes with eight or fewer headings list every title. Longer notes show two neighbors each side of the current heading plus a tick rail of the whole file, and a wrap seam when the jump loops."
config:
  flowchart:
    rankSpacing: 12
    nodeSpacing: 16
    wrappingWidth: 260
---
flowchart TD
  Q{{"`**How many headings?**`"}}
  SHORT["`**Full outline**<br/>every title`"]
  LONG["`**Window of five**<br/>two before, current, two after`"]
  RAIL["`**Tick rail**<br/>one mark per heading`"]
  WRAP["`**Wrap seam plus chip**<br/>when the jump loops`"]
  Q -->|"8 or fewer"| SHORT
  Q -->|"9 or more"| LONG
  LONG --> RAIL
  SHORT --> RAIL
  RAIL --> WRAP
  classDef decision fill:#FFF7E6,stroke:#C77C02,stroke-width:1.5px,color:#4A3000
  classDef focus fill:#E8F1FB,stroke:#3B78C2,stroke-width:1.5px,color:#0F2E52
  classDef outcome fill:#E7F5EC,stroke:#2E7D4F,stroke-width:1.5px,color:#123D24
  class Q decision
  class SHORT,LONG focus
  class RAIL,WRAP outcome
